# sys-frontier-boundary. The Battle Frontier's plaza and lobbies load and are walkable.
# A constructed start in the plaza; each of the five facilities is entered from the plaza and its single-battle
# receptionist asked. The Battle Tower is real (its own sys-tower-* replays): here its receptionist's
# menu is left with B. The other four end on the decomp's own decline:
# the Hall, Castle and Arcade check the party with a stub that answers "not enough" (call_battle_*_function 0), so
# the receptionist prints the ROM's not-eligible message (message_seen_banlist_species, real); the Factory (rentals, no
# party check) heals, then asks to save (the in-script save is real since F1) and B declines, which ends the challenge. No battle, no warp but the lobby doors, no hang; back out to the plaza each time.
# Generated with a shortest-path walker (see tests/integration/m6-turnback.rom.test.ts), checked by m6-systems.
party 0 platinum:SPECIES_GARCHOMP 60 platinum:MOVE_EARTHQUAKE platinum:MOVE_DRAGON_CLAW
party 1 platinum:SPECIES_EMPOLEON 60 platinum:MOVE_SURF
party 2 platinum:SPECIES_LUXRAY 60 platinum:MOVE_THUNDERBOLT
set flag platinum:FLAG_GAME_COMPLETED true
date 2009-03-22 12:00
warp platinum:MAP_HEADER_BATTLE_FRONTIER 48 51 up
until idle
# The Battle Tower.
+0 press up
until position 48 18 300
+0 release up
+0 press up
until state player.zone "platinum:MAP_HEADER_BATTLE_TOWER" 300
+0 release up
advance text 3000
until idle 600
+0 press up
until position 15 6 300
+0 release up
+8 press up
+2 release up
+8 press a
+1 release a
advance text 3000
